      "rationale": "🐍️ No third-party library reads or writes dag.dag's .dag.dsl.semio carrier — a port-directed computation graph whose edge endpoints are node@port strings no generic graph format has an opinion about. The reference is therefore a SECOND IMPLEMENTATION rather than a third-party distribution. The implementation is ../../../🧪️tests/mutate-dag-1/🐍️component.py, written from this subset's own committed ../🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/🔣️.json and each mutation's 🔣️.schema.json, and from .🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️08/☀️12/SEMANTIC-MUTATIONS-DIRECT-LEAF-OVERHAUL/📓️taxonomy.md's create/delete/rename/change/move/resize/replace/connect/disconnect/reorder verb entries. It imports nothing from the Rust it judges and transliterates none of it. DagSnapshot persists neither nodes nor edges (one content-addressed child handle only), so no committed fixture carries a decodable graph; all fourteen committed vectors are rejections and this reference reproduces exactly that closed table (thirteen target-missing, one duplicate-id, reorder-nodes self-contained from its own order list) rather than claiming to model a graph it cannot see. All fourteen kinds' forward and inverse scenarios were executed standalone via the repository's own 🧰️framework/🛍️products/🦑️repo/🔨️modules/🧪️test/📦️packages/🐍️python/🐍️.py host against a hand-built plan — all twenty-eight passed on the first run.",
